  "privacyTitle": "Privacy Policy",
  "privacyBody": "Parrot Trainer is developed by DimonSmart. It uses the microphone to detect sounds during a training session and lets you record training phrases. Phrase text, recordings, settings, and statistics are stored in Android app-private storage.\n\nThe app has no developer-operated backend, advertising, analytics, or crash-reporting SDK. It does not sell your data. Phrase recordings are excluded from Android cloud backup; settings and statistics may be included in Android system backup if backup is enabled on your device.\n\nAndroid's selected speech-recognition provider may process or transmit audio according to its own privacy policy. The selected Android text-to-speech provider processes phrase text, and some voices may use network processing under that provider's policy.\n\nLocal data remains until you delete it, clear the app's storage, or uninstall the app. Data that stays on the device is protected by Android's application sandbox. For privacy questions, use the support contact on the Google Play listing."
